Chapter: TlsCertTest
  cites Encode chapter TlsCert
  cites Encode chapter X509
  cites Foreword chapter Tls
  cites Foreword chapter Ed25519
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Certificate and CertificateVerify, RFC 8446 sections 4.4.2 and 4.4.3.

 The signed content is checked against bytes built independently, outside
 Codex, straight from the spec text: 64 spaces, the ASCII context string,
 one zero, then the transcript hash. A round-trip test cannot catch a wrong
 context string or a CCE-encoded one, because the signer and the verifier
 make the same mistake and agree with each other. That is exactly how the
 TLS key schedule shipped every label in CCE.

 The keypair is RFC 8032 section 7.1 TEST 2 -- published, not minted here.

